ic IP → 35.172.xxx.xxx (value logged).\\n    1.3 Assign hostname \\\"app01\\\"; tag for cost-allocation.\\n    1.4 DNS  (Route 53 or external registrar)\\n        • A-record  @  → Static IP\\n        • CNAME  www → @\\n    1.5 HTTPS  (bncert-tool)\\n        • Include both root + www.\\n        • Auto-renew cron installed by bncert.\\n    1.6 Nightly automated snapshot schedule; retention = 7 days.\\n    1.7 Export snapshot “baseline-clean” immediately after OS patches.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n2.  CORE SECURITY & HARDENING  (Director of Infrastructure)\\n    2.1 Replace default Bitnami password; save in AWS Secrets Manager secret \\\"hoa/wp-admin\\\".\\n    2.2 Create new WP admin \\\"hoa_admin\\\"; delete \\\"user\\\".\\n    2.3 Enforce HTTPS redirect site-wide via bncert.\\n    2.4 Password Policy\\n        • Install “Password Policy Manager” plugin.\\n        • Settings: min 12 chars, upper+lower+digit+symbol, expiry 365 days.\\n    2.5 Two-factor Authentication\\n        • Install “WP 2FA” plugin.\\n        • Force-enable 2FA for all Administrators & Editors.\\n    2.6 Account Lockout / Brute Force\\n        • Wordfence → Enable extended firewall, lockout after 5 failures/30 min, 4-hour ban, CAPTCHA on login.\\n    2.7 Session Management\\n        • Install “Inactive Logout” plugin → auto-logout after 30 minutes idle.\\n    2.8 Disable XML-RPC completely via “Disable XML-RPC” plugin.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n3.  AUDIT, LOGGING & PRIVACY  (Director of Infrastructure)\\n    3.1 Install “WP Activity Log” plugin; store logs 90 days.\\n    3.2 Forward Apache & auth logs to AWS CloudWatch Logs group “hoa-prod”.\\n    3.3 GDPR / Privacy\\n        • Install “WP GDPR Compliance”.\\n        • Create Privacy Policy page template; enable data-export & delete request form.\\n        • Data retention policy: resident accounts removed 12 months after move-out (manual script).\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n4.  FUNCTIONAL PLUGINS  (Director of WordPress Build)\\n    4.1 Members (member-only access control) → create role “Resident”.\\n    4.2 WPForms Lite + WP Mail SMTP (for contact form) – no-code builder.\\n    4.3 Classic Editor (simpler editing).\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n5.  THEME / UI  (Director of UX & Training)\\n    5.1 Install Astra theme.\\n    5.2 Import starter-site “Charity”.\\n    5.3 Customise logo, palette (provided by board), header/footer.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n6.  CONTENT & ACCESS CONTROL  (Director of WordPress Build)\\n    6.1 Pages\\n        • Public: Home, Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools.\\n        • Protected (Resident): Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (category-protected).\\n    6.2 Use Members plugin: restrict each protected page & News category to role=Resident.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n7.  RESIDENT ACCOUNT ON-BOARDING  (Director of WordPress Build)\\n    7.1 Disable public registration.\\n    7.2 Bulk CSV import via “Import Users from CSV” plugin.\\n    7.3 Script to trigger password-reset e-mail for each new Resident.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n8.  E-MAIL / SMTP  (Director of Infrastructure)\\n    8.1 Amazon SES\\n        • Verify domain myhoa.org.\\n        • DKIM keys auto-generated → add CNAME records.\\n        • SPF record:  \\\"v=spf1 include:amazonses.com ~all\\\".\\n        • DMARC record: \\\"v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:dmarc@myhoa.org\\\".\\n        • Request SES production access in region us-east-1.\\n    8.2 Configure WP Mail SMTP → mailer=SES, region us-east-1, credentials via IAM user “ses-wp” (least privilege).\\n    8.3 Fallback: enable secondary SMTP profile (Gmail API key stored in Secrets Manager) — manual switch if SES fails.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n9.  BACKUP & DISASTER RECOVERY  (Director of Infrastructure)\\n    9.1 Lightsail nightly snapshot (already 1.6).\\n    9.2 Weekly off-site backup: wp-content & DB dump to S3 bucket “hoa-backups” (AES-256-SSE).\\n    9.3 Lifecycle rule → transition to Glacier Deep Archive after 30 days.\\n    9.4 Quarterly restore test on staging instance; log outcome.\\n    9.5 Document restore SOP with RTO=4 hours, RPO=24 hours.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n10. TESTING MATRIX  (Director of Infrastructure & UX joint)\\n     10.1 Functional Access-Control Test Cases\\n          • Anonymous user → protected URL → expect login.\\n          • Resident user → protected URL → success.\\n     10.2 Security\\n          • WPScan full vulnerability scan; remediate High findings.\\n          • Wordfence scan clean.\\n     10.3 Load\\n          • k6 script: 50 virtual users, 10 min steady; target TTFB < 800 ms.\\n     10.4 Cross-browser\\n          • Chrome, Safari, Edge, Firefox latest + iOS/Android via BrowserStack.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n11. USER TRAINING & HANDOVER  (Director of UX & Training)\\n     11.1 Create 5-page PDF user manual with screenshots:\\n           • Logging in & 2FA setup\\n           • Editing a page\\n           • Posting News & Events\\n           • Uploading files (minutes, financials)\\n           • Managing Resident accounts\\n     11.2 Record three ≤3-minute screencast videos (host on unlisted YouTube):\\n           • “Adding a News Post”\\n           • “Uploading Meeting Minutes”\\n           • “Resetting a Resident Password”\\n     11.3 Live 30-minute Zoom walkthrough (optional) – schedule link.\\n     11.4 Deliver credentials archive via 7-zip AES encrypted file; share password verbally.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n12. GO-LIVE  (Chief oversees)\\n     12.1 Switch DNS TTL to 300 seconds, verify HTTPS.\\n     12.2 Send announcement e-mail via SES to all residents.\\n     12.3 Monitor CloudWatch, Wordfence Live Traffic 24 hours.\\n\\n──────────────────────────────────────\\n13. ONGOING MAINTENANCE (document)\\n     • Monthly plugin + core updates (enabled via Wordfence Central auto-upda